course: dictionary
lesson: 1940
title: Commercial: a word with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Commercial whaling killed huge numbers of whales» tells you the whales were hunted to be bought and sold. So commercial means connected with buying and selling, or business and trade.
explain: Read the words next to it. «a ban on commercial whaling» means a rule stopping whales being hunted for money. The ban is the clue: a rule like that is only needed when people are making money from something. Try your meaning in the sentence: "a ban on buying and selling whaling" still makes sense, so the guess fits.
explain: The same word can have other meanings. A very commercial film is a film made to earn money rather than for art or kindness. A commercial on TV is an advert, and that is a noun, so check whether the word is describing something or naming something.
fact: Commercial is mostly an adjective. It describes a noun, as in commercial whaling or commercial flights.
fact: «Commercial» means connected with buying and selling, business or trade.
fact: «Commercial» can also mean made to earn money rather than for art or kindness, as in a very commercial film.
fact: «A commercial» is a noun: an advertisement on TV or radio.
fact: After a ban on commercial whaling in 1986, many humpback whale groups grew strongly.
exercise: «Commercial whaling killed huge numbers of whales.» What does commercial mean here? | *Connected with buying and selling | Made at home for fun | Kind and gentle | Very quiet
exercise: «A commercial» is on TV, trying to persuade people to buy something. What is a commercial? | A kitchen used by a business | A kind of whale | A type of art | *An advertisement on TV or radio
exercise: «Humpbacks grew strongly after a ban on commercial whaling in 1986.» What did the ban stop? | *Whales being hunted to be sold | Whales singing long songs | Ships sailing at night | People watching whales from boats
test: «Her new film was very commercial, made just to earn money.» What does commercial suggest? | Made only for art and kindness | Made under the sea | Made by a child at home | *Made to earn money rather than for art
test: «Commercial flights» carry passengers. What does commercial mean here? | Flights of birds in the sky | *Run by businesses to carry people for money | Flights for play and fun | Flights of stairs in a house
exam: «Commercials try to persuade you, so think before you believe them.» What is a commercial? | A rule about buying whales | *An advert on TV or radio that tries to persuade you | A whale that sings long songs | A kitchen used only at home
